Problem: Prod box is misbehaving (high CPU, NGINX 5xx, disk almost full).
Goal: A CLI that (1) inspects the system & logs, 
(2) summarizes likely root causes, 
(3) retrieves your runbooks/best-practices via RAG, 
(4) generates safe, reviewable Bash fixes as a script.


Synopsis:

Shows plain LLM vs LLM + LangChain + RAG difference clearly.

Uses shell + Python realistically.

Reinforces runbooks as the “knowledge base” that powers RAG.


-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------


Process flow :

Collect: script tails logs (nginx/syslog), grabs top/disk stats.

LLM only: ask Mistral to explain likely causes & suggest fixes.

RAG pass: retrieve matching runbooks (your .txt/.md) with FAISS; re-ask Mistral with that context → safer, policy-aligned fixes.

Output: show side-by-side plans; write shell_fix.sh with commands (commented & idempotent).

Student review: dry-run; then bash shell_fix.sh if approved.



